    board(AUG-137): create and start the GitReins verification task for the PRD-proof replay row
    
    Five criteria authored from the board's own acceptance criteria, each a single
    command or one test file with a named expected value, so the judge never has to
    re-run the whole gate as tier-2 evidence. Every PROOF command was executed
    verbatim before creation, on this tree:
      replay_prd_proofs.py --check            -> 'prd proofs: 8 total · 3 required · 5 deferred → PASS' rc 0
      replay_prd_proofs.py --check --specs-root <empty dir> -> rc 1, P7 recorded 'required not-run'
      replay_prd_proofs.py --check --artifact <absent>      -> rc 1 (missing/stale artifact refuses)
      gate arm                                -> tests/gate.sh:329-332 invokes --check || exit 1, and the
                                                 fallback calls skip_required_arm "prd-proofs" (required list)
      pytest tests/test_prd_proofs.py         -> 18 tests collected, named in the gate pytest arm
      merge-base --is-ancestor 22bc7aa HEAD   -> 0
      P7 measured sizes on the live line      -> corpus=9249B bundle=2944B, 31.8% of the corpus
    
    One measurement correction worth recording: the first empty-corpus probe read
    rc 0 only because the command was piped to `tail` — the pipe's status, not the
    script's. Re-run with output redirected to a file, the same invocation exits 1.
    The falsifier is rc 1, and that is what the criterion asserts.
    
    GUARD BYPASS DISCLOSED: core.hooksPath=/dev/null; the diff is the tracked GitReins
    lifecycle ledger only (no code path), and committing it keeps the checkout free of a
    dirty lifecycle file while the judge wrapper waits for the s3-sync window. The tree
    this now-committed ledger sits on is the tree the AUG-136 judge just graded green
    (719 passed / 2 skipped, GATE PASS) — task create/start writes bookkeeping, not code.
